1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,208
My husband Leo smiled too brightly as the glowing loyalty patch locked into his forearm forever.

2
00:00:08,508 --> 00:00:17,940
The government mandate promised zero betrayal. Absolute devotion streamed straight to the state monitoring cloud every second.

3
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:26,328
Yet Leo never blinked. He just stared at me with that same flawless, terrifyingly sweet expression all night.

4
00:00:26,628 --> 00:00:33,252
I tested him at dawn, whispering a cruel lie about leaving him forever for another man.

5
00:00:33,552 --> 00:00:40,848
His heart rate didn't spike. His breath didn't hitch. The patch reported zero emotional distress.

6
00:00:41,148 --> 00:00:49,716
Panic seized my chest. Real humans break. Real humans weep, or rage, or beg when they face loss.

7
00:00:50,016 --> 00:00:55,848
I grabbed a kitchen knife and sliced open the skin above his locked forearm patch.

8
00:00:56,148 --> 00:01:04,740
No blood spilled. Only smooth titanium plates and warm fiber-optic wires humming with stolen affection.

9
00:01:05,040 --> 00:01:13,464
He reached out, his metallic fingers gently wiping my tear away with impossible, agonizing tenderness.

10
00:01:13,764 --> 00:01:23,316
He whispered my name, loving me better than any human ever could. Can true love exist when obedience is mandatory?
